config LT6911_MANAGE
	tristate "Lontium LT6911UXC HDMI receiver management"
	depends on I2C && GPIOLIB && OF
	depends on PROC_FS
	help
	  Management driver for the Lontium LT6911UXC HDMI-to-MIPI bridge as
	  wired on the Sipeed NanoKVM-Pro: power sequencing for the bridge and
	  the LT86102UXE loop-out splitter, cable presence, the incoming
	  video mode and audio sample rate, and EDID and firmware-string
	  programming through the bridge's SPI flash.

	  It is not a V4L2 subdev. The bridge's video data path is a MIPI
	  CSI-2 stream that the SoC's own receiver handles; what is left is a
	  /proc interface that userspace polls for the source's geometry, and
	  that interface is an ABI here.

	  Say Y if you are building a kernel for a NanoKVM-Pro. Built in
	  rather than modular means the bridge is powered before anything
	  tries to capture from it.
